      "date": "2026-07-23",
      "description": "US National Average Gas Price Jumps to $4.09/gallon",
      "details": "The national average price for a gallon of regular gasoline surged by 15 cents in one week, reaching $4.09. This increase pushed prices in most states to $4 per gallon or higher. Rising crude oil prices, attributed to volatility in the Strait of Hormuz and regional instability, were cited as the cause. For a DTC food gifting brand, higher gas prices typically suppress discretionary spending, leading to lower ROAS and higher CPA as consumers prioritize essential purchases over gifts.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "AAA Newsroom"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "description": "Conference Board Consumer Confidence Falls to 90.8 in July",
      "details": "The Conference Board Consumer Confidence Index decreased by 1.4 points to 90.8 in July, down from an upwardly revised 92.2 in June. The Present Situation Index fell for the third consecutive month, and the Expectations Index remained below the recessionary 80.0 threshold. This indicates growing consumer pessimism about current and future economic conditions, likely due to ongoing geopolitical tensions and inflation concerns. Reduced consumer confidence generally leads to a decrease in discretionary spending, negatively impacting ROAS and increasing CPA for premium gifting brands.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "The Conference Board"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-31",
      "description": "UofM Consumer Sentiment Rises to 55.2 in July, Inflation Expectations Dip",
      "details": "The final University of Michigan Consumer Sentiment Index for July rose to 55.2, an 11.5% increase from June's 49.5, marking a five-month high. This improvement was broad-based across demographics and linked to easing gas prices. Year-ahead inflation expectations also ticked down to 4.2% from 4.6% in June. Improved consumer sentiment and slightly lower inflation expectations can boost discretionary spending, leading to higher ROAS and lower CPA for gifting brands.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "boosts_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "University of Michigan"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-08-06",
      "description": "Meta Ads Reporting Breakdowns Require Opt-In, Causing Data Gaps",
      "details": "As of August 6, 2026, Meta's Ads Insights API began requiring an opt-in for impression_device, hourly-stats, and frequency_value breakdowns. This change means that requests from non-enabled accounts return empty data arrays, leading to dashboards showing zeroes instead of errors. For advertisers, this can create temporary blind spots in performance analysis, making it harder to optimize campaigns. The lack of granular data can hinder quick adjustments, potentially leading to inefficient ad spend and negatively impacting ROAS and CPA until data access is restored.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "platform",
      "icon": "🔴",
      "mood_impact": "neutral",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "AdMake AI Blog"
    },
    {
